# Structures, prepared inputs and poses. Everything under data/ is either
# downloaded by scripts/02_fetch_benchmarks.sh or written by a later stage,
# so none of it is tracked. data/README.md says what belongs there and where
# it comes from. On the machine this was developed on, data/ is a pointer to
# a directory on a larger filesystem; see project.conf.
data/*
!data/README.md

# Docking inputs and outputs. PDBQT files are intermediates that
# scripts/06_dock.sh deletes once the pose and the score have been read into
# the results table; these rules are here so that a killed run cannot leave
# one staged by accident.
*.pdbqt
*.pdbqt.gz

# Pose archives. Top-N poses per run are written as gzipped SDF. Across
# every dataset, arm and method these total more than the rest of the
# repository put together, and they are regenerable from the manifests.
*.sdf.gz
*.sdf.zst
poses/

# Structure downloads from the RCSB. Re-fetchable from the accessions in
# config/, which are tracked.
*.pdb
*.cif
*.cif.gz
*.ent.gz
*.mmtf
*.mmtf.gz

# Conda environment directories and the package cache, if either is ever
# created inside the repository rather than under the conda root.
envs/
.conda/
conda-env/
*.conda
*.tar.bz2

# project.conf is written by scripts/00_configure.sh for one machine: thread
# count, memory ceiling, disk budget, absolute paths, tool locations. Every
# clone regenerates its own.
project.conf

# Per-stage logs. The timing and resource tables next to them are tracked,
# because the README quotes numbers out of them.
logs/*.log
logs/*.done
logs/tmp/

# Quarto and Jupyter build artefacts. The rendered report is kept.
*.html
!results/report/*.html
*_files/
.quarto/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
